msgid "Running specific tests"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus provides the ability to limit test execution to tests with specific  "
"`@TestProfile` annotations.\n"
"This works by leveraging the `tags` method of `QuarkusTestProfile` in "
"conjunction with the `quarkus.test.profile.tags` system property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Essentially, any `QuarkusTestProfile` with at least one matching tag "
"matching the value of `quarkus.test.profile.tags` will be considered active\n"
"and all the tests annotated with `@TestProfile` of active profiles, will be "
"run while the rest will be skipped.\n"
"This is best shown in the following example."
msgstr ""

msgid "First let's define a few `QuarkusTestProfile` implementations like so:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Now let's assume that we have the following tests:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Let's consider the following scenarios:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.test.profile.tags` is not set: All tests will be executed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.test.profile.tags=foo`: In this case none of tests will be executed "
"because none of the tags defined on the `QuarkusTestProfile` implementations "
"match the value of `quarkus.test.profile.tags`.\n"
"Note that `NoQuarkusProfileTest` is not executed either because it is not "
"annotated with `@TestProfile`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.test.profile.tags=test1`: In this case `SingleTagTest` and "
"`MultipleTagsTest` will be run because the tags on their respective "
"`QuarkusTestProfile` implementations\n"
"match the value of `quarkus.test.profile.tags`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.test.profile.tags=test1,test3`: This case results in the same tests "
"being executed as the previous case."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.test.profile.tags=test2,test3`: In this case only "
"`MultipleTagsTest` will be run because `MultipleTagsTest` is the only "
"`QuarkusTestProfile` implementation whose `tags` method\n"
"matches the value of `quarkus.test.profile.tags`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Conditional test execution based on application configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus provides `@EnabledIfConfig` and `@DisabledIfConfig` annotations to "
"conditionally enable or disable tests based on application configuration.\n"
"These work similarly to JUnit's https://docs.junit.org/6.1.2/writing-tests/"
"conditional-test-execution.html[`@EnabledIfSystemProperty` and "
"`@DisabledIfSystemProperty`], but resolve values through the full "
"MicroProfile Config system.\n"
"This means that any registered `ConfigSource` is consulted, including "
"`application.properties`, system properties, environment variables, and any "
"custom config sources."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both annotations accept the following attributes:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`named` — the configuration key to look up"
msgstr ""

msgid "`matches` — a regular expression to match against the resolved value"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`disabledReason` (optional) — a custom reason to display when the test is "
"skipped"
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@EnabledIfConfig</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@EnabledIfConfig` enables a test only when the specified configuration key "
"exists and its value matches the given regular expression.\n"
"If the key is not defined, the test is **disabled**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The test class is enabled only when `my.feature.enabled` resolves to `true`."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can also apply the annotation to individual methods:"
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@DisabledIfConfig</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@DisabledIfConfig` disables a test when the specified configuration key "
"exists and its value matches the given regular expression.\n"
"If the key is not defined, the test remains **enabled**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The optional `disabledReason` provides context when the test is skipped."
msgstr ""

msgid "Repeatable annotations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Both annotations are `@Repeatable` and can be stacked on the same class or "
"method, but the evaluation semantics differ:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Multiple `@EnabledIfConfig`**: the test is enabled only when **all** "
"conditions match (AND semantics). If any single condition does not match, "
"the test is disabled."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Multiple `@DisabledIfConfig`**: the test is disabled when **any** "
"condition matches (OR semantics). The first matching condition disables the "
"test."
msgstr ""

msgid "Nested Tests"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JUnit https://docs.junit.org/current/writing-tests/nested-tests.html[@Nested "
"tests] are useful for structuring more complex test scenarios.\n"
"However, note that it is not possible to assign different test profiles or "
"resources to nested tests within the same parent class."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mock Support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus supports the use of mock objects using two different approaches. You "
"can either use CDI alternatives to\n"
"mock out a bean for all test classes, or use `QuarkusMock` to mock out beans "
"on a per test basis."
msgstr ""

msgid "CDI <code>@Alternative</code> mechanism."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To use this simply override the bean you wish to mock with a class in the "
"`src/test/java` directory, and put the `@Alternative` and `@Priority(1)` "
"annotations on the bean.\n"
"Alternatively, a convenient `io.quarkus.test.Mock` stereotype annotation "
"could be used.\n"
"This built-in stereotype declares `@Alternative`, `@Priority(1)` and "
"`@Dependent`.\n"
"For example if I have the following service:"
msgstr ""

msgid "I could mock it with the following class in `src/test/java`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Overrides the `@Dependent` scope declared on the `@Mock` stereotype."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is important that the alternative be present in the `src/test/java` "
"directory rather than `src/main/java`, as otherwise\n"
"it will take effect all the time, not just when testing."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that at present this approach does not work with native image testing, "
"as this would require the test alternatives\n"
"to be baked into the native image."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mocking using QuarkusMock"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `io.quarkus.test.junit.QuarkusMock` class can be used to temporarily "
"mock out any normal scoped\n"
"bean. If you use this method in a `@BeforeAll` method the mock will take "
"effect for all tests on the current class,\n"
"while if you use this in a test method the mock will only take effect for "
"the duration of the current test."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This method can be used for any normal scoped CDI bean (e.g. "
"`@ApplicationScoped`, `@RequestScoped` etc, basically\n"
"every scope except `@Singleton` and `@Dependent`)."
msgstr ""

