msgid ""
"The test code itself can be easily debugged with any of the well known "
"methods (like launching the test from the IDE, adding `-Dmaven.failsafe."
"debug` if the test is launched via Maven, etc.),\n"
"but the application under test needs to have the necessary flags passed to "
"it via `quarkus.test.arg-line` to enable debugging. For testing an "
"application\n"
"packaged as *jar*, you can use:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"as an argument to Maven/Gradle when launching the test. This will make the "
"application wait until a remote JVM debugger is connected to port `5005`."
